     comm(1), join(1), uniq(1)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ssoorrtt utility is compliant with the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”)
     specification, except that it ignores the user's locale(1) and always as‐
     sumes LC_ALL=C.

     The flags [--ggHHhhiiMMRRSSssTTVVzz] are extensions to that specification.

     All long options are extensions to the specification.  Some are provided
     for compatibility with GNU ssoorrtt, others are specific to this implementa‐
     tion.

     Some implementations of ssoorrtt honor the --bb option even when no key fields
     are specified.  This implementation follows historic practice and IEEE
     Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”) in only honoring --bb when it precedes a key
     field.

     The historic practice of allowing the --oo option to appear after the _f_i_l_e
     is supported for compatibility with older versions of ssoorrtt.

     The historic key notations ++_p_o_s_1 and --_p_o_s_2 are supported for compatibil‐
     ity with older versions of ssoorrtt but their use is highly discouraged.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     A ssoorrtt command appeared in Version 1 AT&T UNIX.

