CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     This implementation of ssoorrtt has no limits on input line length (other
     than imposed by available memory) or any restrictions on bytes allowed
     within lines.

     The performance depends highly on efficient choice of sort keys and key
     complexity.  The fastest sort is on whole lines, with option --ss.  For the
     key specification, the simpler to process the lines the faster the search
     will be.

     When sorting by arithmetic value, using --nn results in much better perfor‐
     mance than --gg so its use is encouraged whenever possible.

